{"The end variable is incorrectly calculated using slotStartTime instead of slotEndTime, which fails to ensure the entire slot duration fits within the working hours.": 0.992715060710907, "Strict equality === between Dayjs objects compares object references, not their date values, causing the condition to always be false. Should use the .isSame() method instead.": 0.9845628142356873, "The logic using dateOverrides.find is flawed when multiple overrides exist for the same day - if a slot is within one override but outside another on the same day, find will return the first override where the slot is 'outside', incorrectly marking the slot as unavailable. Should filter for all overrides on the relevant day and check if the slot fits within any of them.": 0.9192069172859192, "Using workingHours.find with a condition that returns true when a slot is outside a range will fail for users with multiple working hour ranges on the same day (e.g., split shifts) - if the slot is in the second range, it will be found 'outside' the first range and incorrectly return false.": 0.9385848045349121, "Performing a .find() on userAvailability inside a loop that iterates over availableTimeSlots results in O(N \u00d7 M) complexity - should create a Map of user IDs to their availability objects before the loop for better performance.": 0.5421645641326904}